1. Coupling lemma of a single flip: y_t = 3^(a_t) x_t + b_t; merge iff the Collatz word of y_1 begins 1^r 0 0
====================================================================================================
  ok: for 3000 random odd v < 2^400 the identity y_t = 3^(a_t) x_t + b_t (four-case chain from (a,b) = (1,2)) and parity(x_t) = parity(y_t) + b_t hold at every step until a_t = 0 (up to 250 steps); whenever the word of y_1 begins 1^r 0 0 the orbits merge exactly at time r+3 (1531 merges)
  ok: exact merge law: among the 2^15 odd classes v mod 2^16, exactly 2^14 - 1 have a word of y_1 beginning 1^r00 with r+2 <= 15 (Haar probability 1/2 in the limit; under the tilted measure Q it is 1-c = 0.3691)
